# Apple signing credentials — NEVER commit. These are private keys: an App
# Store Connect key (AuthKey_*.p8) and a signing certificate bundle
# (cert.p12) sit untracked in the repo root during notarization work, and
# publishing either to a public repo cannot be undone by deleting the commit.
# Matched by extension rather than by filename so a rotated or renamed key is
# still caught.
*.p8
*.p12

# Rust build artifacts (~1.7 GB — never commit these)
/target

# macOS system files
.DS_Store

# Xcode user-specific state (not project configuration)
xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/

# Compiled static library produced by the Cargo build phase — regenerated on
# every Xcode build; committing it would bloat the repo with binary churn.
frontends/SparkampMac/libsparkamp_macos.a

# Vendored dependencies (cargo vendor)
/vendor/

# Flatpak build artifacts
/flatpak-cargo-generator.py
/repo/
/build-dir/
/.flatpak-builder/
/Sparkamp.flatpak
# Test bundles exported for cross-distro checks (Sparkamp-crosslinux-test.flatpak
# and friends) — build artefacts, rebuilt on demand, never committed.
/Sparkamp-*.flatpak

# Development / scratch files
dev.txt

# Test media files — copyrighted, must never reach GitHub
/Testing/

# Built distribution artifacts (DMGs, installers) — too large for git
/dist/

# Per-developer macOS xcodebuild export config (generated/edited locally)
packaging/macos/export-options.plist

# Signing / notarization credentials — NEVER commit these.
*.p12
*.p8
AuthKey_*.p8

# Other large binaries not needed in the repo
*.wsz
*.mp3
*.jpg
*.png
!square logo.png
!frontends/SparkampMac/Assets.xcassets/**/*.png
# Test fixtures are the exception: they are a tenth of a second of sine tone
# each, generated by tools/make-test-tones.sh, and the tag and probe tests
# cannot run without them. tone.mp3 was silently excluded by the *.mp3 rule
# above, so tests/tag_write_containers.rs passed on the machine that made it
# and failed on every fresh clone.
!tests/fixtures/*.mp3
